<title>UK: Algerian Sonatrach cuts Mar LPG to $195/$215 a ton.</title>
<headline>Algerian Sonatrach cuts Mar LPG to $195/$215 a ton.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Algerian state oil and gas company Sonatrach has cut its official posted prices for Liquefied Petroleum Gas (LPG) for March.</p>
<p>Propane falls to $195 a tonne for material loading at Bethioua, a drop of $140 a tonne from February's level of $335.</p>
<p>Butane is down to $215 a tonne, a fall of $75 from the February level of $290 a tonne.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom, +44 171 542 6412</p>
